Machine-level English reading of dqrls.x86-64.disasm.txt
===================================================

Source: ../dqrls.x86-64.disasm.txt
Historical x86-64 ELF disassembly; instruction addresses in the standalone
object are not absolute linked addresses. This is a first-pass annotated
concordance of printed instruction starts and encodings; individual prose
is NOT a verified state-transformer implementation.

Every INSTRUCTION line is machine-byte evidence followed by a long English
operation name and an operand-specific explanatory sentence. A relocation
is included on the same record. In normal non-branching execution the next
execution index is the byte address of the following instruction, not the
number of the next displayed line. See accompanying machine-state document.

No claim is made that all displayed branches were executed or that code
inside external shared libraries is present here.

INSTRUCTION 0001 | 0x0 | 41 57 | push   r15
  Section or entry point: dqrls_.
  Long operation: Allocate an eight-byte stack slot and save a value.
  Detailed first-pass effect: Evaluate the complete original value of r15, including any source memory address using the pre-decrement stack pointer. Decrease RSP by 8; store that eight-byte value at memory address RSP. The instruction can fault. Flags are unchanged.
  Sequential successor if not otherwise redirected or faulting: 0x2 (2 bytes).
  Link-time relocation: none.

INSTRUCTION 0002 | 0x2 | 31 c0 | xor    eax,eax
  Section or entry point: dqrls_.
  Long operation: Write the bitwise exclusive-or result and update logic condition flags.
  Detailed first-pass effect: The same register eax is both operands: write zero to the encoded-width destination (and zero-extend a 32-bit register write), while updating zero/sign/parity flags, clearing carry/overflow and leaving auxiliary-carry undefined.
  Sequential successor if not otherwise redirected or faulting: 0x4 (2 bytes).
  Link-time relocation: none.

INSTRUCTION 0003 | 0x4 | 49 89 cf | mov    r15,rcx
  Section or entry point: dqrls_.
  Long operation: Copy one operand's exact-width value without performing arithmetic.
  Detailed first-pass effect: Read rcx at the width indicated by this encoding and write the resulting bit pattern to r15. If this writes a 32-bit general register, its encompassing 64-bit register has its upper 32 bits cleared. A memory read/write is observable; condition flags do not change.
  Sequential successor if not otherwise redirected or faulting: 0x7 (3 bytes).
  Link-time relocation: none.

